---- PART A: recentre the fold changes ----
Three versions of the same fit, differing only in how the lineage-wide offset is handled.
  raw      : bMIND estimates as they are
  post-hoc : t recomputed as (logFC - median logFC) / SE, same SEs  [diagnostic]
  per-sample: each sample's median across genes removed BEFORE fitting  [principled]

  gran  raw       median -0.1184 |  7.6% up |   109 at BH 0.05 (17 up, 92 down)
        post-hoc  median +0.0000 | 50.0% up |    89 at BH 0.05 (85 up, 4 down)   (shift removed -0.1184)
        per-samplemedian +0.0086 | 54.4% up |   284 at BH 0.05 (203 up, 81 down)

  mono  raw       median -0.0163 | 31.1% up |    20 at BH 0.05 (19 up, 1 down)
        post-hoc  median +0.0000 | 50.0% up |    24 at BH 0.05 (23 up, 1 down)   (shift removed -0.0163)
        per-samplemedian +0.0011 | 51.4% up |   162 at BH 0.05 (136 up, 26 down)

  T     raw       median -0.0124 | 38.4% up |    28 at BH 0.05 (26 up, 2 down)
        post-hoc  median -0.0000 | 50.0% up |    45 at BH 0.05 (43 up, 2 down)   (shift removed -0.0124)
        per-samplemedian -0.0034 | 46.7% up |   278 at BH 0.05 (206 up, 72 down)

  NK    raw       median -0.0006 | 47.9% up |     4 at BH 0.05 (3 up, 1 down)
        post-hoc  median -0.0000 | 50.0% up |     4 at BH 0.05 (3 up, 1 down)   (shift removed -0.0006)
        per-samplemedian -0.0004 | 48.7% up |    96 at BH 0.05 (89 up, 7 down)

  B     raw       median -0.0105 |  6.3% up |     0 at BH 0.05 (0 up, 0 down)
        post-hoc  median +0.0000 | 50.0% up |     3 at BH 0.05 (3 up, 0 down)   (shift removed -0.0105)
        per-samplemedian -0.0003 | 48.4% up |   158 at BH 0.05 (109 up, 49 down)

