---- PART C: filter on across-sample standard deviation ----
The filter statistic is each gene's SD across all samples within a lineage, computed
IGNORING GROUP. That independence is what makes filtering legitimate (Bourgon 2010):
it cannot bias the group test under the null. The check is printed below.

  independence check -- Spearman(SD, p-value) among genes with p > 0.5:
    gran  rho = -0.0016  (n = 4635)   independent
    mono  rho = +0.0045  (n = 4927)   independent
    T     rho = -0.0050  (n = 4808)   independent
    NK    rho = -0.0388  (n = 5397)   independent
    B     rho = +0.0024  (n = 4276)   independent

